<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hunza-Nagar Campaign</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1891</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Anglo-Brusho War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hunza-Nagar Campaign was a British expedition of December 1891 led by Colonel Algernon Durand against the states of Hunza and Nagar in the Karakoram. After the storming of the fort of Nilt, in which three Victoria Crosses were won, both states submitted and came under the supervision of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilgit-agency">Gilgit Agency</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hunza-nagar-campaign.jpg" alt="Hunza-Nagar Campaign" width="320" height="436" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Graphic · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Fighting_near_Gilgit_on_the_North-Western_Frontier_of_India,_1891.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
